data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1681,"item_id":"fc_0851639458e1939b016adb68c4537481918fd0f976af9b77f0","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"target_review\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The frozen target expands contextually to the exact approved statement: parameters n:ℕ and E⊆ℝⁿ; H001 nonempty and H002 compact; I=[0,1], concatenated Euclidean metric; conclusion P supplies the equality. This corresponds to the approved n=d−1, d≥1 exercise. Empty E is deliberately excluded; n=0 is included. The conclusion need not duplicate globally supplied parameter/H context. The literal source exercise lacks nonemptiness, but frozen-target/source-context record the approved strengthened test target and why it is needed.\",\"locations\":[\"frozen-target.md:7-17\",\"problem.md:3\",\"source-context.md:12-20\",\"spec.json:4-27,101-105\"]},\"definition_reviews\":{\"D001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"volume is explicitly the standard real Lebesgue measure, with no asserted theorem or hidden property. Its uses are within the stated domain.\",\"locations\":[\"spec.json:28-40\",\"nl0.json:490-505\"]}},\"source_reviews\":{\"M001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Complete signature has EMetricSpace, MeasurableSpace, BorelSpace and the strict NNReal-exponent inequality. Source proves exactly the infinite-measure conclusion; actual use is stated in R001.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:2-30\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:107-118\",\"nl0.json:27-70\"]},\"M002\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full source telescope includes measurable space, measure, Countable β, and AEMeasurable summands. The proposition accurately states the ENNReal tsum-integral identity. No reliance is evident in the sole inference; retained as unused direct input.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:32-60\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean:360\",\"nl0.json:73-130\"]},\"M003\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature matches: Borel extended metric structures and dimH(A)<↑d imply Hausdorff measure zero. Actual source lines establish exactly this. Application-specific audit remains part of the flawed, monolithic R001 argument.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:62-90\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:130-135\",\"nl0.json:144-188\"]},\"M004\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Complete telescope requires EMetricSpace on source and target and LipschitzWith K f; conclusion is image dimension ≤ source dimension. Restatement faithful.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:92-120\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:94-98\",\"nl0.json:190-244\"]},\"M005\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature includes NormedAddCommGroup, NormedSpace ℝ, FiniteDimensional, and nonempty interior. The displayed restatement is faithful to that result.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:122-150\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:10-11\",\"nl0.json:247-288\"]},\"M008\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full application formula matches the source, including real exponent, positive scale, countable cover, diameter bound and nonempty-set supremum. It is a theorem rather than a definition.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:152-180\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Hausdorff.lean:546-552\",\"nl0.json:290-348\"]},\"M009\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature requires pointwise f≤g for ENNReal functions on a measurable measure space; restatement matches.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:182-210\",\"nl0.json:350-408\"]},\"M010\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature includes MeasurableSet S and arbitrary ENNReal c and gives the indicator integral identity. Faithful restatement.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:212-240\",\"nl0.json:410-467\"]},\"M011\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Source signature accurately states volume(Icc a b)=ofReal(b−a), with no hidden hypotheses beyond real endpoints. Its use is conditional on the erroneous local interval construction in R001.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:469-506\"]},\"M012\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Complete signature requires the same three extended-metric/measurable/Borel structures and non-top Hausdorff measure; implication to dimH≤↑d matches source theorem.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:509-552\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:123-124\"]},\"M013\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature includes OuterMeasureClass/FunLike structure and A⊆B; statement is a faithful abstraction of monotonicity.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:554-601\"]},\"M014\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature has extended metric, measurable and Borel structures; measure=top implies ↑d≤dimH. Restatement faithful.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:603-647\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:126-128\"]}},\"structure_review\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"There is a single inference R001 directly producing P; all listed propositions lie in its direct-input set, so the visible graph is structurally closed at this level, but the argument does not establish the target. In particular local declaration A_i (type projection of V_i to ℝⁿ) says instead 'Define ν=volume.restrict([0,1])', which declares no A_i and does not define ν's asserted type. More substantively, R001's lower-bound route constructs covers and interval enclosures and invokes a purported product-measure/cover-cost estimate without a proved derivation; the listed M sources do not establish that estimate. M002, for example, only exchanges a countable tsum with a lintegral under AEMeasurability, which does not itself prove the geometric lower bound. Witness U_{j,i} also claims an arbitrary countable cover with small cost from zero Hausdorff measure and compactness without supplying the required cover construction/replacement details. Thus AND closure cannot be granted for R001/P. No packet replay was performed or fabricated.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:650-677\",\"nl0.json:806-818\",\"nl0.json:958-977\",\"nl0.json:989-1266\"]},\"findings\":[{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"R001 does not provide a justified lower-bound implication from its stated inputs to dim_H(E×I)≥dim_H(E)+1. It relies on a product-cover/measure estimate not proved in the visible argument and not supplied by its M inputs. This blocks P and the whole proof.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:650-677\",\"nl0.json:989-1266\"]},{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Object declaration mismatch: A_i is declared as the projection of V_i, but its declaration text defines ν=volume.restrict([0,1]); these are different objects/types and the declaration does not define A_i.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:806-818\"]},{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The alleged c_s witness is a Hausdorff content value, but the declaration claims an enclosing interval J_i and cites M008 as its existence basis. M008 is only the Hausdorff-measure covering formula and does not prove existence of that interval; the declaration/basis do not support the stated witness.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:850-880\"]},{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The actual applications are embedded in a single extremely long R001 argument and no separate fresh packet replay was performed. Source signature fidelity was reviewed where source text was available; this does not count as inference replay.\",\"locations\":[\"references/audit-a.md:149-161\",\"nl0.json:650-677\"]}]}}"}

